# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# Every comment here is on its own line, and that is not a matter of taste:
# in .gitignore a '#' only starts a comment at the start of a line. A trailing
# comment becomes part of the pattern, so the rule then matches a filename
# nobody has and ignores nothing at all. Nine rules in this file were broken
# that way — including the one for the API keys, the TLS private key and a
# linked WhatsApp session.
# your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
# the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp
# account, not just a key
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
# Google OAuth client secrets
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
# your appointments, and the .ics files written for them
memory/calendar/
# audio JARVIS generated to send you
memory/voice_notes/
# which server-side conversation this desktop is continuing
memory/conversation_state.json
memory/*.db

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
/build/
/dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
/logs/
/downloads/
/screenshots/

# ── JARVIS Command Center ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
command_center/.env
# ...but the documented example must stay in the repository
!command_center/.env.example
command_center/frontend/node_modules/
command_center/frontend/dist/
# built by `npm run build` / the Docker image
command_center/backend/static/
# sqlite db, workspace, secret.key
data/
